    "title": "The spring buying surge that never quite translated to closings - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Liezel Once ,\n1 days ago The spring homebuying season attracted more engaged buyers than the market had seen in years, yet sales told a far more modest story, according to new data from Zillow. A September Zillow analysis found that engaged home shoppers — defined as Zillow users who saved or shared a for-sale listing, signaling real intent beyond casual browsing — reached 4.8 per listing nationally during the second quarter, a 21% jump year over year. Read full article",
